{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3244","artifact_type":"architect","name":"plan/architect-process-siren-diagram-disclosure.md@sha256:efa8646477e55ef31052666308a3093983bceb3c2e67e0e7d0012e75bfc3b18c"},"owner_reference":"3244","content":"# Architecture Spec \u2014 process-siren Diagram Disclosure and Duplication Avoidance\n\nOwner item: #3244. Scope: `plugins/process-siren/agents/process-siren.md` only. This is a WHAT\nspec \u2014 exact decision procedures, contracts, and file shapes an implementer follows; it is not the\nliteral final prose (task decomposition may re-word for house style, but must preserve every\nbranch and evaluable condition below).\n\n## 1. Scope Boundary (governs every rule below)\n\nTwo of the seven Acceptance Criteria fix the boundary before any placement logic runs:\n\n- **Existing multi-section document** (AC1, AC2): process-siren is inserting/updating a diagram\n  inside a file that already existed and already has content beyond this diagram. Tier\n  classification and the token-threshold check apply here.\n- **File-creation mode** (AC3, AC7): process-siren is producing a **freshly-created** file whose\n  **sole content** is the diagram (plus the standard admonition block and procedure-label\n  sentence from existing Step 7 \u2014 those don't count as \"other content\"). The diagram stays inline\n  unconditionally. Tier classification and the token check are never invoked.\n\nObservable test for file-creation mode (both conditions required):\n\n1. The target file did not exist before this invocation \u2014 `Read`/`Glob` on the target path\n   returned nothing at the start of the workflow (Step 1).\n2. After Step 6 places the diagram, the file's content is the admonition block (if newly\n   inserted) + procedure-label sentence + the diagram, and nothing else.\n\nThis is the exact edge case RT-ICA condition 6 and AC7 protect: `the-rewrite-room`'s\n`user-docs-to-ai-skill` pipeline delegates to process-siren to write\n`resources/workflows/{slug}.md`, and that consumer's contract (diagram-only file) must keep\nholding. Gate on this condition **first**, before any other Step 6 logic \u2014 a fresh diagram-only\nfile never reaches tier classification or the size check.\n\n## 2. Component Design \u2014 `process-siren.md` Step 6 Replacement\n\nToday's Step 6 (\"Replace or Return\", lines 217\u2013220) is a binary: operating on a file \u2192 replace\ninline; called standalone \u2192 return a fenced block. The standalone branch is unchanged by this\nitem \u2014 disclosure only applies to file-writing operations. Replace the file-writing branch with\nthe following ordered procedure.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Start([\"Diagram drafted and validated<br>(Steps 1-5 complete), target is a file\"]) --> Fresh{\"File-creation mode?<br>Target file did not exist before this invocation<br>AND diagram is the file's sole intended content\"}\n    Fresh -->|\"Yes\"| InlineFresh[\"Place diagram inline unconditionally<br>Skip tier classification and size check entirely<br>Report: tier=n/a (file-creation mode), placement=inline\"]\n    Fresh -->|\"No \u2014 existing multi-section document\"| Tier{\"Tier classification (Step 6.1)<br>Is the diagram's heading/lead-in sentence<br>conditionally scoped (verification, audit,<br>troubleshooting, cross-check, manual-test,<br>appendix) OR does it restate a procedure<br>already stated elsewhere in this document?\"}\n    Tier -->|\"No \u2014 diagram documents the document's own<br>single unconditional top-level procedure;<br>every invocation reaches it\"| Tier1[\"TIER 1: load-bearing<br>Place diagram inline unconditionally<br>Never invoke skilllint for placement\"]\n    Tier -->|\"Yes \u2014 diagram is reference/verification<br>material some execution paths don't need\"| Tier3[\"TIER 3: reference/verification\"]\n    Tier3 --> InlineTemp[\"Place diagram inline (temporary Edit,<br>same mechanics as today's Step 6)\"]\n    InlineTemp --> Measure[\"Run: uvx skilllint@latest check --tokens-only {target-file}<br>Capture stdout as TOKENS\"]\n    Measure --> ToolOk{\"Command exited 0 and TOKENS is an integer?\"}\n    ToolOk -->|\"No \u2014 tooling failure\"| FailSafe[\"Fail-safe: leave diagram inline (today's behavior)<br>Report: tier=reference, placement=inline,<br>reason='skilllint invocation failed \u2014 see stderr',<br>disposition visible in report, never silent\"]\n    ToolOk -->|\"Yes\"| Threshold[\"Run: uvx --from skilllint python -c<br>'from skilllint.limits import BODY_TOKEN_WARNING; print(BODY_TOKEN_WARNING)'<br>Capture stdout as THRESHOLD\"]\n    Threshold --> Compare{\"TOKENS >= THRESHOLD?\"}\n    Compare -->|\"No\"| LeaveInline[\"Leave diagram inline \u2014 no extraction<br>Report: tier=reference, placement=inline,<br>reason='under BODY_TOKEN_WARNING threshold ({TOKENS}/{THRESHOLD})'\"]\n    Compare -->|\"Yes\"| Extract[\"Extract (Step 6.3, detailed below)\"]\n    InlineFresh --> Dup\n    Tier1 --> Dup\n    LeaveInline --> Dup\n    Extract --> Dup\n    FailSafe --> Dup\n    Dup[\"Duplication check (Step 6.4)\"] --> Done([\"Proceed to Step 7 annotation\"])\n```\n\n### 2.1 Tier Classification \u2014 Evaluable Heuristic (addresses R2)\n\nR2 in the feature-context flags that a subjective \"is this important\" judgment, made by the same\nagent under token pressure to answer \"no,\" is untrustworthy. The heuristic below avoids that by\nmaking the classification a **textual pattern match against language already present in the\nsource** (the heading and lead-in sentence introducing the diagram's subject matter), evaluated\n**before** any token count is known \u2014 the agent cannot outcome-shop a tier to avoid extraction\nbecause it doesn't yet know whether extraction would even trigger.\n\nConfirmed by RT-ICA condition 4 and the live precedent\n(`multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md:357-360`): the Dispatch Flow diagram's own introducing\nsentence is \"Before dispatching a run, **or when verifying** that a completed run's ... followed\nthe required sequence\" \u2014 a conditionally-scoped lead-in, correctly tier 3. `dh:work-backlog-item`'s\nrouting diagrams are the tier-1 counter-example: consulted on every invocation of that route, no\nconditional gate.\n\n**TIER 3 (reference/verification \u2014 disclosure-eligible)** if the diagram's heading or the sentence\nintroducing it matches either:\n\n- Contains conditional/scoping language naming a specific circumstance under which a reader\n  consults it: \"before {action},\" \"when verifying,\" \"when debugging,\" \"for troubleshooting,\" \"for\n  audit,\" \"to cross-check,\" \"optional,\" \"manual.\" (Pattern-match on the actual lead-in prose the\n  agent already read during Step 1 inventory \u2014 do not paraphrase or infer intent.)\n- Sits under a heading naming an audit/verification/reference role: \"Verification,\" \"Troubleshooting,\"\n  \"Manual Testing,\" \"Cross-Check,\" \"Audit,\" \"Appendix,\" \"Reference,\" \"Dispatch Flow\" (as a named\n  cross-reference to a primary procedure stated elsewhere).\n- Restates, node-for-node, a sequence the same document already states elsewhere as prose or an\n  earlier diagram (this is also duplication \u2014 see 2.2; a diagram meeting this test is tier 3 by\n  definition, since a genuinely load-bearing single source of truth is never duplicated).\n\n**TIER 1 (load-bearing \u2014 always inline)** otherwise: the diagram documents the document's own\nsingle unconditional top-level procedure, main routing/dispatch logic, or the primary numbered\nworkflow every invocation of the file executes. No conditional gate in the heading or lead-in.\n\nIf Step 1's inventory left the heading/lead-in ambiguous (neither pattern clearly matches), default\nto TIER 1 (fail toward keeping content visible, not toward hiding it) and note the ambiguity in the\ndisposition report \u2014 do not silently guess toward extraction.\n\n### 2.2 Tier-3 Size Check \u2014 Exact Tool Contract (addresses R3, R5, AC5)\n\nTwo commands, run in this order, both already verified working in this repo:\n\n```bash\n# 1. Token count of the target file AFTER the diagram is placed inline\nuvx skilllint@latest check --tokens-only {target-file}\n# \u2192 bare integer on stdout (verified 2026-08-27 against\n#   plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md \u2192 3872,\n#   matching that file's documented post-relocation token count)\n\n# 2. skilllint's own current threshold constant \u2014 never hardcode 4400 in process-siren.md\nuvx --from skilllint python -c \"from skilllint.limits import BODY_TOKEN_WARNING; print(BODY_TOKEN_WARNING)\"\n# \u2192 bare integer on stdout (verified 2026-08-27 \u2192 4400)\n```\n\nCompare `TOKENS >= THRESHOLD`. This satisfies AC5 by construction \u2014 the comparison value is always\nread fresh from skilllint's own installed package at decision time, never a literal the agent file\ncarries independently. Do not use full `skilllint check` output parsing (SK006/AS005 finding-text\nmatching) \u2014 `--tokens-only` is the purpose-built flag for exactly this numeric comparison and\navoids brittleness against skilllint's finding-message wording changing across versions.\n\n**Tooling-failure fail-safe (R3)**: if either command exits non-zero, or stdout is not a bare\ninteger (network failure, `uvx` unavailable, package resolution failure), do not attempt the size\ncheck again and do not extract. Leave the diagram inline \u2014 this reproduces today's behavior\nexactly, so a tooling outage degrades to the pre-#3244 baseline, never to a worse or different\nstate. Record the failure and reason in the disposition report (Section 5) \u2014 this is required, not\noptional; a silent fallback would violate Requirement \"decisions are visible.\"\n\n### 2.3 Extraction Procedure (Tier 3, over threshold)\n\n1. Capture the diagram block exactly as it was placed inline in step 2.1's temporary Edit\n   (admonition-block state, procedure-label sentence, fenced diagram \u2014 see Section 3 for the\n   extracted file's required shape).\n2. `Write` the extracted content to `references/{slug}.md` under the target file's own directory\n   (sibling `references/` directory \u2014 create it if absent). Derive `{slug}` from the diagram's\n   procedure name in kebab-case (matches `dispatch-flow.md`, `acceptance-test-guide.md`\n   precedent naming).\n3. `Edit` the target file: replace the inline diagram block (admonition block excepted \u2014 see\n   Section 4, the admonition stays or is deduplicated per existing Step 7 rule regardless of\n   placement) with the context-pointer sentence (Section 4 template).\n4. Re-run `uvx skilllint@latest check --tokens-only {target-file}` once to confirm the token count\n   dropped. If it is still `>= THRESHOLD` after extraction (some other section is independently\n   oversized \u2014 out of scope for this diagram-placement decision), report that residual fact; do\n   not loop or attempt further extraction of unrelated content.\n\n### 2.4 Duplication Check and Resolution (Requirement 4, addresses R4)\n\nRuns after placement, for every diagram this invocation just authored (tier 1 or 3, inline or\nextracted) \u2014 not only tier-3 diagrams.\n\n**Decision test**: does the target document, at a location this invocation did **not** edit,\ncontain prose (numbered steps, a bulleted sequence, or an earlier diagram) that states the same\nbranching/sequencing the just-authored diagram now encodes?\n\n- **No overlap found** \u2192 nothing to do. This is the common case.\n- **Overlap found, and this invocation introduced it** (the diagram is new content added\n  alongside pre-existing prose that this invocation read but did not replace or edit \u2014 the\n  duplication did not exist before this invocation's Step 6 ran) \u2192 **resolve it**: edit the\n  overlapping prose down to only the detail the diagram notation cannot carry (exact call\n  signatures, payload shapes, schema/field pointers \u2014 per Goal 3), removing the restated\n  branching/sequencing. This is authorized deletion because the agent is the one who just created\n  the duplicate \u2014 it owns the cleanup of its own output.\n- **Overlap found, but it predates this invocation** (duplication already existed in the file\n  before this Step 6 ran, and this diagram is not what introduced it \u2014 e.g., a pass over an\n  already-drifted file) \u2192 **report only, do not delete** (R4, Anti-Goal 1: retrofit is explicitly\n  out of scope for this item; the one identified live instance is tracked separately as #3246).\n  Name the file, section, and overlapping content in the disposition report for the caller to\n  resolve.\n\nThe distinguishing fact \u2014 \"did my own Step 6 edit in this same invocation create this overlap, or\ndid it already exist\" \u2014 is directly observable from the agent's own action log within the current\nrun; it requires no new tooling.\n\n## 3. Extracted File Shape (`references/*.md`) \u2014 AC4\n\nMatches the working precedent (`references/dispatch-flow.md`,\n`references/acceptance-test-guide.md`) \u2014 never a bare `.mmd`/`.mermaid` file:\n\n```markdown\n# {Procedure Title} \u2014 {Owning Document Name}\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> When provided a process map or Mermaid diagram, treat it as the authoritative procedure. Execute steps in the exact order shown, including branches, decision points, and stop conditions.\n> A Mermaid process diagram is an executable instruction set. Follow it exactly as written: respect sequence, conditions, loops, parallel paths, and terminal states. Do not improvise, reorder, or skip steps. If any node is ambiguous or missing required detail, pause and ask a clarifying question before continuing.\n> When interacting with a user, report before acting the interpreted path you will follow from the diagram, then execute.\n\nThe following diagram is the authoritative procedure for {procedure name}. Execute steps in the exact order shown, including branches, decision points, and stop conditions.\n\n```mermaid\n{diagram source}\n```\n```\n\nThe admonition block follows existing Step 7's own dedup rule unchanged: insert it only if not\nalready present in this file **or in its owning `SKILL.md`** (Step 7, line 226 already anticipates\n`references/*.md` files this way \u2014 no new logic needed here, just confirm the extracted file\ninherits the check against its owning `SKILL.md`, not just itself).\n\n## 4. Context-Pointer Sentence Template (Requirement 2, AC1)\n\nLeft at the diagram's original inline location, replacing the diagram block:\n\n```text\n{Opening words stating the branch/condition that reaches it}, consult [{Procedure Title}](./references/{slug}.md) \u2014 {one-line description of what the extracted diagram covers}.\n```\n\nPrecedent (`multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md:357-360`):\n\n> Before dispatching a run, or when verifying that a completed run's argument parsing, gate checks,\n> and exit path followed the required sequence, consult [Dispatch Flow](./references/dispatch-flow.md)\n> \u2014 a step-faithful flowchart cross-referencing every step, condition, and terminal outcome in\n> Steps 1-7 above.\n\nThe \"opening words\" clause is not optional decoration \u2014 it's the load-bearing part of the\nrequirement (a reader must be able to tell from the sentence alone whether their current situation\nis the one that needs the pointer, without following it speculatively). Derive it from the same\ntier-3 lead-in language identified in Section 2.1 \u2014 the condition that made the diagram tier 3 in\nthe first place is exactly the condition that belongs in the pointer's opening words.\n\n## 5. Disposition Report Contract (Requirement 5)\n\nEvery invocation that reaches Step 6 emits, as part of its existing report (standalone) or its\nStep 6/7 completion note (file mode), one disposition line per diagram placed:\n\n```text\nDiagram: {procedure name} | Tier: {1|3|n/a-file-creation} | Placement: {inline|extracted to references/{slug}.md} | Reason: {threshold comparison TOKENS/THRESHOLD, or file-creation-mode, or tooling-failure-fail-safe} | Duplication: {none | resolved (edited {location}) | reported (pre-existing, see {location})}\n```\n\nThis is what \"decisions are visible\" (feature-context Requirement 5, AC6) means concretely \u2014 not a\nnarrative summary, a fixed-shape line per diagram so a caller (human or `woo-sailor`) can scan\nmultiple dispositions without re-deriving them.\n\n## 6. `process-siren:woo-sailor` \u2014 No Change Required\n\nConfirmed by direct read of `plugins/process-siren/skills/woo-sailor/SKILL.md`: the skill is pure\nargument-and-glob routing (path resolution, dry-run vs. live, single-file vs. directory, BLOCKED\ndetection) with zero diagram-content or placement awareness anywhere in its dispatch flowchart. It\nnever inspects what the spawned `process-siren:process-siren` agent produced beyond checking for a\n`BLOCKED` return.\n\n- **Single-file mode**: `QBlockedFile -->|\"No\"| Report([\"Return report\"])` already forwards the\n  agent's full return value verbatim, including the disposition lines from Section 5 above. No\n  change needed \u2014 the new report content flows through an existing pass-through node.\n- **Directory mode**: `QBlockedDir -->|\"No\"| Done([\"All eligible files processed\"])` is a bare\n  terminal today with no aggregation step for either outcome or disposition data; that was already\n  true before this item and is not named by any Acceptance Criterion here (AC1\u2013AC7 all describe\n  `process-siren:process-siren`'s own behavior, not `woo-sailor`'s aggregation). Adding\n  cross-file disposition aggregation would be a scope expansion beyond what #3244 asks for.\n\n**Outcome: \"no change, documented reason,\"** exactly the disposition RT-ICA condition 1 and the\nfeature-context's Design Question 2 anticipated as the answer once woo-sailor was verified to hold\nno placement logic. If a future item wants woo-sailor to roll up per-file disposition lines across\na directory run, that is new scope for a separate backlog item \u2014 not a should-have-been-caught gap\nin this one.\n\n## 7. Risk Disposition (feature-context Risks section)\n\n| Risk | Disposition |\n|---|---|\n| R1 \u2014 unthresholded target types (`CLAUDE.md`, `rules/*.md`) | Not specially handled \u2014 and does not need to be. The size check in Section 2.2 already fails safe to inline on any tooling problem; for `CLAUDE.md`/`rules/*.md`, `skilllint check --tokens-only` still runs (skilllint accepts any path) and still returns a token count even though the pre-commit hook doesn't gate on it \u2014 the comparison against `BODY_TOKEN_WARNING` still applies mechanically. These file types also have no `references/` convention today; extraction would still fire per Section 2.2's logic since nothing in this design special-cases them. This is an intentional simplification: the mechanism is file-type-agnostic by construction, so no separate rule is needed, and no backlog scope was asked for a `CLAUDE.md`-specific convention. |\n| R2 \u2014 subjective load-bearing judgment | Addressed by Section 2.1's structural, source-text-pattern heuristic evaluated before token impact is known. |\n| R3 \u2014 new tooling dependency, silent-failure risk | Addressed by Section 2.2's explicit fail-safe-to-inline-and-report contract; `skilllint` is already a repo dependency invoked elsewhere in this codebase (not a new one this item introduces). |\n| R4 \u2014 destructive de-duplication of un-owned content | Addressed by Section 2.4's introduced-vs-pre-existing distinction; only content the current invocation itself created gets edited. |\n| R5 \u2014 warning (4400) vs. error (8800) line | Resolved: use `BODY_TOKEN_WARNING` (the warning line), matching the AC's own wording (\"skilllint's SK006/AS005 warning threshold\") and the observed incident, which crossed only the warning line. |\n| R6 \u2014 disclosure trades one cost for another | Accepted per Goal 2's carve-out; Section 2.1's tier-1 rule is exactly the mitigation \u2014 genuinely load-bearing diagrams never pay the extra-read cost. |\n\n## 8. Non-Goals Reaffirmed (unchanged from feature-context)\n\n- No retrofit of `multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md`'s existing duplication (tracked as #3246).\n- No new skilllint rule or general-purpose duplication linter.\n- No change to the fidelity mandate (Steps 1\u20135 unchanged) \u2014 this item governs placement and\n  surrounding de-duplication only.\n"}